menu "FTM time responder"

config FTM_TIME_RESPONDER
    bool "Put a gPTP Follow_Up in every FTM frame (bridge)"
    depends on HOSTED_AVB_CLOCK_LINK && !FTM_CLOCK_PROBE
    default n
    help
        The access point side of 802.1AS FTM time transfer: the
        coprocessor, the FTM responder, puts a Follow_Up in every FTM frame
        it sends a station esp_ptp has admitted, giving gPTP time at that
        frame's measurement. The host feeds it gPTP time on the
        coprocessor's clock-link timer every 200 ms. Enable on both the
        bridge and its coprocessor, with HOSTED_AVB_CLOCK_LINK on both;
        the coprocessor also needs CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_ENABLE_FTM_PTP
        (Espressif's PTP compatible FTM). The bridge logs the
        coprocessor's counts every 10 s (FTMRESP lines).

config BEACON_TIME_FROM_LINK
    bool "Fill the beacon time element for one instant (bridge)"
    depends on HOSTED_AVB_CLOCK_LINK
    default n
    help
        The coprocessor writes gPTP time at the very AP TSF the beacon
        time element carries, from the host's gPTP time on its clock-link
        timer, and the rate of gPTP time against the TSF in the element's
        cumulativeScaledRateOffset. Without it the host stamps the element
        and the coprocessor adds the TSF a host message later, with a
        rate of 0, and stations follow it through a slow envelope. Enable
        on both the bridge and its coprocessor, with HOSTED_AVB_CLOCK_LINK
        on both. The coprocessor logs BEACONTIME lines every 10 s.

config BEACON_TIME_OFFSET_NS
    int "Added to the beacon element's gPTP time (ns)"
    depends on BEACON_TIME_FROM_LINK
    range -1000000 1000000
    default 64000
    help
        A constant the filled element's gPTP time is advanced by. Without
        it a station behind esp-ap ran 64 us behind wired gPTP on the
        scope (11-23, sd 1.9 us over 27 min): the latency between the
        AP TSF read here and the TSF the station takes the time against.

config FTM_TIME_TRANSFER
    bool
    default y if FTM_TIME_RESPONDER || BEACON_TIME_FROM_LINK

endmenu
